# =============================================================================
# Build-context ignore rules for deploy/docker/Dockerfile.* (context = repository root).
#
# Every image build (compose, the release, security and helm workflows) uses the repository root
# as its context, so this is the one file Docker applies. There is no per-Dockerfile copy.
# =============================================================================

# Version control and editors
.git
.github
.vs
.vscode
.idea
**/*.user
**/*.swp

# Build output — everything is rebuilt inside the image
**/bin
**/obj
**/out
**/artifacts
**/publish
**/TestResults
**/*.binlog
**/BenchmarkDotNet.Artifacts

# Node: fetched with npm ci in the spa stage; dist is produced there
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.vite
**/*.tsbuildinfo
src/Dle.Control/wwwroot/admin

# Not needed for either image. LICENSE and NOTICE stay in the context: both runtime stages of
# each image copy them to /app/licenses/.
tests
docs
sdk
deploy/aspire
deploy/helm
deploy/postgres
deploy/*.yml
deploy/.env
deploy/.env.*
deploy/Caddyfile
deploy/geoip
*.md

# Local secrets and databases
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/secrets.json
**/*.mmdb
**/*.pfx
**/*.key
**/*.pem
